                note: "Same net as iCE40 pin 23. Keep it at 3.3 V logic (FPGA pin absolute max 3.6 V, though the RP2350 pad alone takes 5 V while IOVDD is powered) and never let gateware drive pin 23 while the RP2350 does. Until the FPGA is configured, pin 23 holds a weak pull-up (11-128 uA). RP2350 erratum E9, only on a chip marked A2 (A3 and A4 fix it): an input-enabled pad left between VIL and VIH sources about 120 uA and sticks near 2.2 V, which the internal pull-down cannot overcome. Use an external pull-down of 8.2k or less, or the pull-up, or enable the pad\'s input only while reading it.",
            ),
